'''Marjcorzo''' ({{Literal translation|meadow of the {{W|Pampas deer|deer}}|}}; {{Langx|mxi|مَرْجْكُورْثُو|Marjkórzo}}) is a [[Regions of Balisca|region]] in northern [[Bayara]], and one of the [[Regions of Balisca|seven regions of the community]]. It borders the [[Estuaria|Estuarian]] regions [[Quiscosta]], [[Mesopotàmia]] and [[Canyars]] to the north, [[Trás-as-Montanyas]] ([[Hesperia]]) to the east, and [[Abellesia]] to the south.

Marjcorzo is almost entirely within the [[Western Plains (Balisca)|Bayaran northern plain]], and generally consists of lowland plains and low hills. The western third of the region consists of the Bayaran Delta. The region has a {{W|humid subtropical climate}}, characterized by hot, humid summers and mild to cool winters. 

